It adds \`BatchSessions\` and shared batching code for both persistent layouts. A batch loads the checkpoint once, writes multiple sessions, rebuilds the summary once, creates one commit, and updates the ref once.

What remains is wiring \`PostCommit\` and \`process_sessions\` to group sessions and call \`BatchSessions\`. So item 2 is still open, but the storage half is already in #2131. If @sdshah09 takes it, we should coordinate around that PR to avoid doing the same work twice.

#2131 does not touch item 2b. That is still separate.`;
